    "text": "```python\ndef starts_one_ends(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return the count of the numbers of n-digit\n    positive integers that start or end with 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(10**n):\n        if i[-10] == '1' or i[0] == '1':\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```\n\nThis function iterates through all possible n-digit numbers and checks if they start or end with 1. If they do, it increments the count.",
